From d5314c95d24149fe425a7d548613afb924fed6bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 337/488] soh: name the 13 address-named symbols defined in
 z_demo_ec.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 13 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Demo_Ec/z_demo_ec.c.

  * func_8096D594 -> DemoEc_MoveActor
    deduced, confidence HIGH: enables root-motion on the skeleton and queues
    the animation system's actor move; the most-used of the three
    near-identical movement helpers.

  * func_8096D5D4 -> DemoEc_MoveActorRebased
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the same move, but first rebases the
    skeleton's translation onto the current root joint so the actor does not
    jump when the animation is swapped.

  * func_8096D64C -> DemoEc_MoveActor2
    deduced, confidence HIGH: a third copy of DemoEc_MoveActor at its own
    address, byte-identical to it and used by five of the update modes.

  * func_8096F1D4 -> DemoEc_UpdateEyesAfterFrame32
    deduced, confidence HIGH: holds eye texture 3 for the first 32 frames of
    the animation and runs the ordinary blink afterwards.

  * func_8096F224 -> DemoEc_SetupUpdate17
    deduced, confidence HIGH: loads the animation object, starts
    gDemoEcAnim_006930 and switches this Carpenter to update mode
    EC_UPDATE_17.

  * func_8096F26C -> DemoEc_AdvanceToUpdate18
    deduced, confidence HIGH: when the current animation has finished it
    starts gDemoEcAnim_006220 and moves on to EC_UPDATE_18.

  * func_8096F2B0 -> DemoEc_CheckCueForUpdate17
    deduced, confidence HIGH: watches this Carpenter's actor cue and, on cue
    2, enters update mode 17.

  * func_8096F378 -> DemoEc_Update17
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the EC_UPDATE_17 body: steps the animation,
    moves the actor, holds the eyes for the first 32 frames and advances to
    mode 18 when the animation ends.

  * func_8096F3D4 -> DemoEc_Update18
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the EC_UPDATE_18 body: steps the animation,
    moves the actor and runs the ordinary blink.

  * func_8096F4FC -> DemoEc_SetupUpdate20
    deduced, confidence HIGH: loads the animation object, starts
    gDemoEcAnim_008D1C and switches to update mode EC_UPDATE_20.

  * func_8096F544 -> DemoEc_AdvanceAnimAfterUpdate20
    deduced, confidence HIGH: starts gDemoEcAnim_009234 once the mode 20
    animation has finished, staying in the same update mode.

  * func_8096F578 -> DemoEc_CheckCueForUpdate20
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the cue watcher for that Carpenter, entering
    update mode 20 on cue 2.

  * func_8096F640 -> DemoEc_Update20
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the EC_UPDATE_20 body: steps the animation,
    moves the actor, blinks, and swaps to the follow-up animation when the
    first one ends.

